<title>UK: Sugar report.</title>
<headline>Sugar report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>LIFFE white sugar futures ended a fairly busy day with prices holding steady at slightly higher levels.</p>
<p>Most of the activity stemmed from switching out of the near August position ahead of its expiry but traders said that some trade buying also helped the overall tone.</p>
<p>At the close prices were between $1.80 and $0.30 a tonne higher and turnover totalled 5,076 lots.</p>
<p>In Paris August 45 ICUMSA ended at $321.50 a tonne, up $2.50 while October 100 ICUMSA was down $1.10 at $287.90 a tonne.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
